$============================================================================
$ Thermodynamic database for the Mo-Si-Y-Hf quaternary system
$
$ Author: Pranav P. S. Setty
$         Department of Materials Science and Engineering
$         The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA 16802, USA
$         pvs5840@psu.edu
$
$ Citation: Setty, P.P.S. (2026). Thermodynamic assessment of the quaternary
$           Mo-Si-Y-Hf system, validated by machine-learning interatomic
$           potentials, and reactive-element co-design of a refractory
$           silicide composite. Computational Materials Science, [in review].
$
$ SCOPE
$   Elements:   MO, SI, Y, HF (with VA sublattice on BCC_A2 and HCP_A3)
$   Phases:     20 (LIQUID, BCC_A2, HCP_A3, DIAMOND_A4, MO3SI, MO5SI3,
$               MOSI2, HF2SI, HF5SI3, HF3SI2, HF5SI4, HFSI, HFSI2, SIY,
$               SI4Y5, ASI5Y3, BSI5Y3, ASI2Y, BSI2Y, SI3Y5)
$   Parameters: 65 Redlich-Kister and end-member coefficients
$   Convention: SGTE unary lattice stabilities (Dinsdale 1991)
$
$ SUBSYSTEM SOURCES
$   Unaries     : Dinsdale 1991 (SGTE), CALPHAD 15(4) 317-425
$   Mo-Si       : Czerny et al. 2024, Adv. Eng. Mater. 26, 2302085
$                 DOI 10.1002/adem.202302085
$   Mo-Hf liquid: Shao 2002, Intermetallics 10(5) 429-434
$                 DOI 10.1016/S0966-9795(02)00017-1
$   Mo-Hf bcc   : Zhao et al. 2020, CALPHAD 69, 101766
$                 DOI 10.1016/j.calphad.2020.101766
$                 Note: Zhao et al. (2020) Table 4 labels the order-1 and
$                 order-2 Redlich-Kister rows as "Mo,Zr" rather than
$                 "Mo,Hf". This is a documented labeling typo; the Mo-Zr
$                 parameters appear separately in Table 5 with different
$                 values, and a sub-regular Redlich-Kister set must belong
$                 to a single binary, confirming all three terms are Mo-Hf.
$   Mo-Y        : Chan et al. 2010, J. Phase Equilib. Diffus. 31(5) 414-420
$                 DOI 10.1007/s11669-010-9753-1
$   Hf-Si       : Zhao et al. 2000, J. Phase Equilib. 21(1) 40-45
$                 DOI 10.1361/105497100770340408
$   Si-Y        : Zhang et al. 2019, CALPHAD 65, 282-290
$                 DOI 10.1016/j.calphad.2019.03.009
$   Hf-Y        : ideal mixing (no published assessment)
$
$ NORMALIZATION
$   Hf-silicides are reported per mole-atom, referenced to GHSERHF (hcp)
$   and GHSERSI (diamond).
$   Y-silicide formation energies in the source were per-formula and have
$   been divided by atom count (SIY/2, SI4Y5/9, *SI5Y3/8) to yield
$   per-mole-atom values consistent with the Hf-silicides
$   (-67 to -80 kJ/mol-atom). The per-formula basis for SIY was inferred
$   from the published value.
$
$ TERNARY AND HIGHER-ORDER INTERACTIONS
$   All ternary and quaternary excess interactions are obtained from the
$   binary subsystems by Muggianu extrapolation. Two matrix-relevant
$   ternary interactions (Mo-Si-Y and Mo-Si-Hf) were computed externally
$   from special quasirandom structure (SQS) relaxations and ESPEI fits;
$   their inclusion shifts the predicted solidus by <=5 K and leaves the
$   phase assemblage unchanged, and they are therefore not embedded in
$   this released database. See manuscript Section 3.5 and Supplementary
$   Figures S14 and S15.
$============================================================================

ELEMENT /-   ELECTRON_GAS              0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00 !
ELEMENT VA   VACUUM                    0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00  0.0000E+00 !
ELEMENT MO   BCC_A2                    9.5940E+01  4.5890E+03  2.8560E+01 !
ELEMENT SI   DIAMOND_A4                2.8085E+01  3.2175E+03  1.8820E+01 !
ELEMENT HF   HCP_A3                    1.7849E+02  5.8450E+03  4.3560E+01 !
ELEMENT Y    HCP_A3                    8.8906E+01  5.9664E+03  4.4434E+01 !

 TYPE_DEFINITION % SEQ *!
 DEFINE_SYSTEM_DEFAULT ELEMENT 2 !
 DEFAULT_COMMAND DEF_SYS_ELEMENT VA /- !

$============================================================================
$ FUNCTION BLOCK
$============================================================================

$---- Unary SER references --------------------------------------------------
$ Mo SER = BCC (Du-Geng [DG], SGTE) -- IDENTICAL to Czerny GHSERMO, no change
FUNCTION GHSERMO  2.98140E+02 -7746.302+131.9197*T-23.56414*T*LN(T)
     -.003443396*T**2+5.66283E-07*T**3+65812*T**(-1)-1.30927E-10*T**4;
      2.89600E+03  Y  -30556.41+283.559746*T-42.63829*T*LN(T)
     -4.849315E+33*T**(-9); 5.00000E+03  N !

$ Si SER = diamond (SGTE/Czerny p.222) -- UPDATED from Du-Geng (+0.0096*T) so the
$ BCC/LIQUID/DIAMOND Si endmembers exactly match Czerny's reference state. [v1]
FUNCTION GHSERSI  2.98140E+02  -8162.609+137.236859*T-22.8317533*T*LN(T)
                   -.001912904*T**2-3.552E-09*T**3+176667*T**(-1);
                   1.68700E+03  Y
                  -9457.642+167.281367*T-27.196*T*LN(T)
                   -4.20369E+30*T**(-9); 3.60000E+03 N !

$ Hf SER = HCP (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0)
FUNCTION GHSERHF  2.73000E+02 -6987.297+110.744026*T-22.7075*T*LN(T)
     -4.146145E-3*T**2-0.000477E-6*T**3-22590*T**(-1); 2.50600E+03  Y
     -1446776.329+6193.609991*T-787.5363829*T*LN(T)+173.5215E-3*T**2
     -7.575759E-6*T**3+501742495*T**(-1); 6.00000E+03  N !

$ Y SER = HCP (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0)
FUNCTION GHSERYY  2.73000E+02 -7347.055+117.532124*T-23.8685*T*LN(T)
     -3.845475E-3*T**2+0.011125E-6*T**3-16486*T**(-1); 1.50000E+03  Y
     -15802.62+229.831717*T-40.2851*T*LN(T)+6.8095E-3*T**2
     -1.14182E-6*T**3; 1.79900E+03  Y
     -72946.216+393.885821*T-58.2078433*T*LN(T)+2.436461E-3*T**2
     -0.072627E-6*T**3+20866567*T**(-1); 6.00000E+03  N !

$---- Phase lattice-stability functions -------------------------------------
$ Si BCC (SGTE) -- references SGTE GHSERSI -> == Czerny G(BCC_A2,SI:VA) absolute
FUNCTION GBCCSI   2.98140E+02 +47000-22.5*T+GHSERSI#; 6.00000E+03 N !

$ Mo HCP (SGTE Dinsdale 1991 convention: +11550-0.222*T over BCC)
FUNCTION GHCPMO   2.98150E+02 +11550-0.222*T+GHSERMO#; 6.00000E+03 N !

$ Si HCP (SGTE Dinsdale 1991 convention: +49200-20.8*T over diamond)
FUNCTION GHCPSI   2.98150E+02 +49200-20.8*T+GHSERSI#; 6.00000E+03 N !

$ Hf BCC (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0)
FUNCTION GHFBCC   2.73000E+02 +5370.703+103.836026*T-22.8995*T*LN(T)
     -4.206605E-3*T**2+0.871923E-6*T**3-22590*T**(-1)-0.1446E-9*T**4;
      2.50600E+03  Y
     +1912456.771-8624.20573*T+1087.6141247*T*LN(T)-286.857065E-3*T**2
     +13.427829E-6*T**3-610085091*T**(-1); 6.00000E+03  N !

$ Y BCC (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0)
FUNCTION GYYBCC   2.73000E+02 +5485.858-20.009726*T+2.927924*T*LN(T)
     -4.150358E-3*T**2+0.747591E-6*T**3-37863*T**(-1)+GHSERYY#; 1.50000E+03  Y
     +13941.422-132.309319*T+19.344524*T*LN(T)
     -14.805333E-3*T**2+1.900536E-6*T**3-54349*T**(-1)+GHSERYY#; 1.75200E+03  Y
     +5594.895-34.089733*T+5.265*T*LN(T)
     -6.8095E-3*T**2+1.14182E-6*T**3+GHSERYY#; 1.79900E+03  Y
     +177760.169-780.053385*T+98.0154419*T*LN(T)
     -22.3552E-3*T**2+0.913936E-6*T**3-52416530*T**(-1)+GHSERYY#; 6.00000E+03  N !

$---- Liquid endmember functions --------------------------------------------
$ Mo liquid (Du-Geng [DG], SGTE) -- == Czerny G(LIQUID,MO), no change
FUNCTION GLIQMO   2.98140E+02 +41831.347-14.694912*T+4.24519E-22*T**7
        +GHSERMO#; 2.89600E+03  Y +34095.373-11.890046*T+4.849315E+33*T**(-9)
        +GHSERMO#; 5.00000E+03  N !

$ Si liquid -- references SGTE GHSERSI -> == Czerny G(LIQUID,SI) absolute
FUNCTION GLIQSI   2.98140E+02 +50696.36-30.099439*T+2.09307E-21*T**7+GHSERSI#;
                   1.68700E+03  Y
                   +49828.165-29.559069*T+4.20369E+30*T**(-9)+GHSERSI#;
                   3.60000E+03 N !

$ Hf liquid (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0 -- absolute expression)
FUNCTION GLIQHF   2.73000E+02 +20414.959+99.790933*T-22.7075*T*LN(T)
     -4.146145E-3*T**2-0.000477E-6*T**3-22590*T**(-1); 1.00000E+03  Y
     +49731.499-149.91739*T+12.116812*T*LN(T)-21.262021E-3*T**2
     +1.376466E-6*T**3-4449699*T**(-1); 2.50600E+03  Y
     -4247.217+265.470523*T-44*T*LN(T); 6.00000E+03  N !

$ Y liquid (mc_ni [MCNI], SGTE/REF:0 -- absolute expression)
FUNCTION GLIQYY   2.73000E+02 +3934.121+59.921688*T-14.8146562*T*LN(T)
     -15.623487E-3*T**2+1.442946E-6*T**3-140695*T**(-1); 1.79900E+03  Y
     -13337.609+258.004539*T-43.0952*T*LN(T); 6.00000E+03  N !

$============================================================================
$ PHASE DECLARATIONS
$============================================================================
PHASE LIQUID  %  1  1.0  !
 CONSTITUENT LIQUID  :MO,SI,Y,HF :  !

PHASE BCC_A2  %  2  1  3  !
 CONSTITUENT BCC_A2  :MO,SI,Y,HF : VA :  !

PHASE HCP_A3  %  2  1  0.5  !
 CONSTITUENT HCP_A3  :MO,SI,Y,HF : VA :  !

PHASE DIAMOND_A4  %  1  1.0  !
 CONSTITUENT DIAMOND_A4  :SI :  !

$ Czerny A.3 simplified silicide models
PHASE MO3SI  %  2  0.77  0.23  !
 CONSTITUENT MO3SI  :MO : SI :  !

PHASE MO5SI3  %  2  0.625  0.375  !
 CONSTITUENT MO5SI3  :MO : SI :  !

PHASE MOSI2  %  2  1  2  !
 CONSTITUENT MOSI2  :MO : SI :  !

$ Hf-silicides [ZHAO 2000] -- stoichiometric line compounds (per mole-atom)
PHASE HF2SI   %  2  0.667  0.333  !
 CONSTITUENT HF2SI   :HF : SI :  !
PHASE HF5SI3  %  2  0.625  0.375  !
 CONSTITUENT HF5SI3  :HF : SI :  !
PHASE HF3SI2  %  2  0.600  0.400  !
 CONSTITUENT HF3SI2  :HF : SI :  !
PHASE HF5SI4  %  2  0.556  0.444  !
 CONSTITUENT HF5SI4  :HF : SI :  !
PHASE HFSI    %  2  0.500  0.500  !
 CONSTITUENT HFSI    :HF : SI :  !
PHASE HFSI2   %  2  0.333  0.667  !
 CONSTITUENT HFSI2   :HF : SI :  !

$ Y-silicides [ZHANG 2019] -- stoichiometric (per-formula G normalized to per-atom; see header note)
PHASE SIY     %  2  0.500   0.500   !
 CONSTITUENT SIY     :SI : Y :  !
PHASE SI4Y5   %  2  0.4444  0.5556  !
 CONSTITUENT SI4Y5   :SI : Y :  !
PHASE ASI5Y3  %  2  0.625   0.375   !
 CONSTITUENT ASI5Y3  :SI : Y :  !
PHASE BSI5Y3  %  2  0.625   0.375   !
 CONSTITUENT BSI5Y3  :SI : Y :  !

$ Si-Y two-sublattice phases [ZHANG 2019] -- v3.1 COMPLETION (alpha/beta-Si2Y + Si3Y5)
PHASE ASI2Y   %  2  2       1       !
 CONSTITUENT ASI2Y   :SI,Y : SI,Y :  !
PHASE BSI2Y   %  2  2       1       !
 CONSTITUENT BSI2Y   :SI,Y : SI,Y :  !
PHASE SI3Y5   %  2  0.375   0.625   !
 CONSTITUENT SI3Y5   :SI,Y : Y :  !

$============================================================================
$ PARAMETER BLOCK
$============================================================================

$---------------------------------------------------------------- LIQUID ----
$ Endmembers
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO;0)  2.98140E+02  +GLIQMO#;  5.00000E+03  N !  $ [DG]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,SI;0)  2.98140E+02  +GLIQSI#;  3.60000E+03  N !  $ [SGTE]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF;0)  2.73000E+02  +GLIQHF#;  6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,Y;0)   2.73000E+02  +GLIQYY#;  6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
$ Mo-Si interaction (4 RK terms) [CZERNY 2024]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -172591.2920+27.6145*T;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,SI;1)  2.98150E+02  +26612.6661-20.6586*T;   6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,SI;2)  2.98150E+02  +38731.7034;             6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,SI;3)  2.98150E+02  +19624.2756;             6.00000E+03  N !
$ Mo-Hf interaction (3 RK terms) [SHAO via MCNI, REF:179]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF,MO;0)  2.73000E+02  -23413-2.27*T;          6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF,MO;1)  2.73000E+02  +46500-28*T;            6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF,MO;2)  2.73000E+02  -0.5*T;                 6.00000E+03  N !
$ Mo-Y interaction (immiscible) [CHAN 2010, JPED 31(5):414-420, DOI 10.1007/s11669-010-9753-1]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,Y;0)  2.98150E+02  +29700;             6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,MO,Y;1)  2.98150E+02  +1500;              6.00000E+03  N !
$ Hf-Si interaction [ZHAO 2000, JPE 21(1) p.40, DOI 10.1361/105497100770340408]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF,SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -177631+6.42546*T; 6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,HF,SI;1)  2.98150E+02  -1830;             6.00000E+03  N !
$ Si-Y interaction [ZHANG 2019, CALPHAD 65 p.282]
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,SI,Y;0)  2.98150E+02  -231878.58;         6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,SI,Y;1)  2.98150E+02  -22570.43+3.00*T;   6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,SI,Y;2)  2.98150E+02  +75072.9-26.56*T;   6.00000E+03  N !
$ GAPS: Hf-Y liquid interaction = ideal (no assessment; no Hf-Y compounds, arXiv:0907.5131).

$---------------------------------------------------------------- BCC_A2 ----
$ Endmembers (..)1(VA)3
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,MO:VA;0)  2.98140E+02  +GHSERMO#;  5.00000E+03  N !  $ [DG]
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,SI:VA;0)  2.98140E+02  +GBCCSI#;   6.00000E+03  N !  $ [SGTE]
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,HF:VA;0)  2.73000E+02  +GHFBCC#;   6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,Y:VA;0)   2.73000E+02  +GYYBCC#;   6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
$ Mo-Si interaction (1 RK term) [CZERNY 2024]
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,MO,SI:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  -114632.1170+26.9372*T;  6.00000E+03  N !
$ Mo-Hf interaction (3 RK terms) [ZHAO 2020 -- DFT-supported beta(BCC), Table 4]
$ DOI 10.1016/j.calphad.2020.101766.
$ Order: HF,MO. Note on Table 4: see source-attribution block in header for
$ the documented labeling typo regarding ;1 and ;2 row identification.
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,HF,MO:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  -24872+8.905*T;   6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,HF,MO:VA;1)  2.98150E+02  +65515-29.9*T;    6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,HF,MO:VA;2)  2.98150E+02  +2159-5.847*T;    6.00000E+03  N !
$ Mo-Y BCC interaction (strongly immiscible, +100 kJ -> expels Y) [CHAN 2010, DOI 10.1007/s11669-010-9753-1]
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,MO,Y:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  +100000;  6.00000E+03  N !
$ GAPS: BCC Si-Hf, Si-Y, Hf-Y interactions = ideal (Si-Hf/Si-Y carried by silicide compounds; Hf-Y no data).

$---------------------------------------------------------------- HCP_A3 ----
$ Endmembers (..)1(VA)0.5 ; Hf/Y are stable references, Mo/Si metastable (SGTE)
PARAMETER G(HCP_A3,MO:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  +GHCPMO#;   6.00000E+03  N !  $ [SGTE]
PARAMETER G(HCP_A3,SI:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  +GHCPSI#;   6.00000E+03  N !  $ [SGTE]
PARAMETER G(HCP_A3,HF:VA;0)  2.73000E+02  +GHSERHF#;  6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
PARAMETER G(HCP_A3,Y:VA;0)   2.73000E+02  +GHSERYY#;  6.00000E+03  N !  $ [MCNI/SGTE]
$ Mo-Y HCP interaction (immiscible, +100 kJ) [CHAN 2010, DOI 10.1007/s11669-010-9753-1]
PARAMETER G(HCP_A3,MO,Y:VA;0)  2.98150E+02  +100000;  6.00000E+03  N !
$ Other HCP interactions = ideal (no data).

$------------------------------------------------------------- DIAMOND_A4 ---
PARAMETER G(DIAMOND_A4,SI;0)  2.98140E+02  +GHSERSI#;  3.60000E+03  N !  $ [SGTE]

$---------------------------------------------------------------- MO3SI -----
$ Czerny A.3 simplified (Mo)0.77(Si)0.23, ABSOLUTE G per mole-atom [CZERNY 2024]
PARAMETER G(MO3SI,MO:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -37759.2536+149.3282*T-26.059*T*LN(T)
   +9.6142E-4*T**2-4.8262E-7*T**3+113220*T**(-1);  6.00000E+03  N !

$---------------------------------------------------------------- MO5SI3 ----
$ Czerny A.3 simplified (Mo)0.625(Si)0.375 (GD8M), ABSOLUTE G per mole-atom [CZERNY 2024]
PARAMETER G(MO5SI3,MO:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -46865+143*T-25.269*T*LN(T)
   +3.2382E-04*T**2-3.9528E-07*T**3+174540*T**(-1);  6.00000E+03  N !

$---------------------------------------------------------------- MOSI2 -----
$ Czerny (Mo)1(Si)2 C11b line compound, ABSOLUTE G per 3-atom formula unit [CZERNY 2024]
PARAMETER G(MOSI2,MO:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -156216.6066+444.2883*T-75.7102*T*LN(T)
   +1.6413E-03*T**2-1.0682E-06*T**3+402589.974*T**(-1);  6.00000E+03  N !

$---------------------------------------------------------------- Hf-SILICIDES [ZHAO 2000] ----
$ Stoichiometric line compounds, per mole-atom; G relative to GHSERHF (hcp) + GHSERSI (diamond).
PARAMETER G(HF2SI,HF:SI;0)   2.98150E+02  -63785+1.5413*T+0.667*GHSERHF#+0.333*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(HF5SI3,HF:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -68537+0.8153*T+0.625*GHSERHF#+0.375*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(HF3SI2,HF:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -76772+2.8296*T+0.600*GHSERHF#+0.400*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(HF5SI4,HF:SI;0)  2.98150E+02  -74987+2.0556*T+0.556*GHSERHF#+0.444*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(HFSI,HF:SI;0)    2.98150E+02  -73013+1.9597*T+0.500*GHSERHF#+0.500*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(HFSI2,HF:SI;0)   2.98150E+02  -69725+10.480*T+0.333*GHSERHF#+0.667*GHSERSI#;  6.00000E+03  N !

$---------------------------------------------------------------- Y-SILICIDES [ZHANG 2019] ----
$ Stoichiometric; per-formula G NORMALIZED to per-atom (divided by atom count) -- see header note.
$ G relative to GHSERSI (diamond) + GHSERYY (hcp). SIY normalization inferred from published per-formula value.
PARAMETER G(SIY,SI:Y;0)     2.98150E+02  -80430.86+1.26*T+0.500*GHSERSI#+0.500*GHSERYY#;     6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(SI4Y5,SI:Y;0)   2.98150E+02  -77663.31+0.35444*T+0.4444*GHSERSI#+0.5556*GHSERYY#; 6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(ASI5Y3,SI:Y;0)  2.98150E+02  -69659.0+2.09125*T+0.625*GHSERSI#+0.375*GHSERYY#;   6.00000E+03  N !
PARAMETER G(BSI5Y3,SI:Y;0)  2.98150E+02  -66990.0-1.5975*T+0.625*GHSERSI#+0.375*GHSERYY#;    6.00000E+03  N !
$---------- Si-Y TWO-SUBLATTICE PHASES [ZHANG 2019, Table 5] -- v3.1 COMPLETION ----------
$ alpha/beta-Si2Y: (Si,Y)2(Si,Y)1 -- end-members per FORMULA (3 atoms); pycalphad -> per-atom (/3).
$ Si3Y5: (Si,Y)0.375(Y)0.625 -- per-atom (site ratios sum to 1). GHSERSI=diamond, GHSERYY=hcp.
$ NOTE: source PDF unavailable; the Table-5 wildcard interaction L(Si,Y:*) and L(*:Si,Y) are
